error[E0277]: a borrowed container of `i64` has no storage of its own type: the container's storage holds the runtime's values, not `i64`s
  --> tests/compile_fail/borrowed_stored_container_at_a_concrete_type.rs:12:1
   |
12 | #[extern_fn(effect = pure)]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this parameter borrows a container of `i64`
   |
   = help: the trait `InPlaceElement<__R>` is not implemented for `i64`
   = note: borrow the elements as a slice: the language's `&[i64]` and `&mut [i64]` are taken as `Slice<Erased<Rt, i64>, Shared, Rt>` and `Slice<Erased<Rt, i64>, Mut, Rt>`, whose elements read in place as `i64` by `as_ref(rt)` and `as_mut(rt)` where `i64: Stored<Rt>`; a `i64` that is itself `TransparentOver<Rt>`, as an `Erased<Rt, X>` is, is taken as `Slice<i64, Shared, Rt>` and `Slice<i64, Mut, Rt>` (RFC-0047).
   = note: a `Vec<i64>` taken by value materializes each element, and an `async` declaration may take one, which it may not a slice.
   = note: a map, a set or a deque is borrowed at the declaration's own type variables, as `&HashMap<K, V, E, Rt>` with `K: Var<kind::Type>`: the runtime keeps it at their run-time instantiation, where each is `Owned<Rt>`.
help: the trait `InPlaceElement<R>` is implemented for `acvus_extern::Owned<R>`
  --> $WORKSPACE/acvus-extern/src/owned.rs
   |
   | / impl<R> crate::InPlaceElement<R> for Owned<R>
   | | where
   | |     R: Runtime,
   | |_______________^
   = note: required for `acvus_ext::HashMap<i64, i64, (), __R>` to implement `Borrowable<__R>`
   = note: required for `ByRef<acvus_ext::HashMap<i64, i64, (), __R>, acvus_extern::Shared>` to implement `for<'a> Arg<'a, __R>`
   = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `extern_fn` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

